1
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:11,260
A class records its screen time at the weekend, in hours.

2
00:00:11,310 --> 00:00:15,580
On Saturday, the boys' average is 4 hours, and the girls' is 3.

3
00:00:15,630 --> 00:00:19,350
On Sunday, the boys' is 5, and the girls' is 4.

4
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:28,210
Which chart compares the boys and the girls, day by day: a dual bar chart, with 2 bars side by side, or a single bar chart of totals?

5
00:00:28,260 --> 00:00:31,410
Pause the video and decide.

6
00:00:31,460 --> 00:00:32,550
A dual bar chart.

7
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:39,070
For each day, there are 2 bars side by side: blue for the boys, and orange for the girls.

8
00:00:39,120 --> 00:00:44,320
You can see at a glance that the boys had more screen time on both days.

9
00:00:44,370 --> 00:00:48,210
Remember: the height of a bar shows the frequency.

10
00:00:48,260 --> 00:00:50,160
Read the scale carefully.

11
00:00:50,210 --> 00:00:54,910
A bar that reaches halfway between 10 and 20 shows 15.

12
00:00:54,960 --> 00:00:59,100
A dual bar chart puts 2 bars side by side for each category.

13
00:00:59,150 --> 00:01:02,790
It uses 2 colours, and a key to explain them.

14
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:07,350
It is good for comparing 2 groups, category by category.

15
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:08,050
Your turn.

16
00:01:08,100 --> 00:01:12,270
On Saturday, the boys had 4 hours and the girls had 3 hours.

17
00:01:12,320 --> 00:01:14,450
What is the total for Saturday?

18
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:17,750
Pause the video and try it.

19
00:01:17,800 --> 00:01:19,200
4 plus 3 is 7 hours.

20
00:01:19,250 --> 00:01:23,340
But the dual bar chart does not show that total directly.

21
00:01:23,390 --> 00:01:26,510
For totals, there is a better chart.

22
00:01:26,560 --> 00:01:31,320
A compound bar chart stacks the groups on top of each other, in 1 bar.

23
00:01:31,370 --> 00:01:34,490
It is also called a stacked bar chart.

24
00:01:34,540 --> 00:01:39,660
The total height shows the whole: 7 hours for Saturday, and 9 for Sunday.

25
00:01:39,710 --> 00:01:42,050
Each section shows a part.

26
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:44,200
To read a top section, subtract.

27
00:01:44,250 --> 00:01:48,840
Take the top of the section, minus the bottom of the section.

28
00:01:48,890 --> 00:01:49,600
Your turn.

29
00:01:49,650 --> 00:01:51,570
A compound bar reaches 40.

30
00:01:51,620 --> 00:01:53,840
Its bottom section reaches 22.

31
00:01:53,890 --> 00:01:55,880
How big is the top section?

32
00:01:55,930 --> 00:01:59,320
Pause the video and try it.

33
00:01:59,370 --> 00:02:01,190
40 minus 22 is 18.

34
00:02:01,240 --> 00:02:04,330
The top section shows 18.

35
00:02:04,380 --> 00:02:05,660
Here is the method.

36
00:02:05,710 --> 00:02:06,710
Step 1: choose.

37
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:09,430
Use a dual bar chart to compare groups.

38
00:02:09,480 --> 00:02:13,480
Use a compound bar chart to show totals and parts.

39
00:02:13,530 --> 00:02:16,730
Step 2: draw the axes with a clear, even scale.

40
00:02:16,780 --> 00:02:18,740
Add labels and a key.

41
00:02:18,790 --> 00:02:23,560
Step 3: for a dual chart, draw 2 bars side by side for each category.

42
00:02:23,610 --> 00:02:26,410
For a compound chart, stack them.

43
00:02:26,460 --> 00:02:31,480
Step 4: to read a stacked section, take the top minus the bottom.

44
00:02:31,530 --> 00:02:36,060
A compound bar shows the vehicles that pass a school on Monday.

45
00:02:36,110 --> 00:02:37,880
The whole bar reaches 32.

46
00:02:37,930 --> 00:02:40,870
The lower section, for bikes, reaches 19.

47
00:02:40,920 --> 00:02:44,770
How many scooters does the upper section show?

48
00:02:44,820 --> 00:02:48,060
Top minus bottom: 32 minus 19 is 13.

49
00:02:48,110 --> 00:02:50,710
There were 13 scooters.

50
00:02:50,760 --> 00:02:57,460
A shop wants to show its total sales for each month, split into online sales and sales in the store.

51
00:02:57,510 --> 00:02:59,760
Which chart should it use?

52
00:02:59,810 --> 00:03:02,290
Both the totals and the parts matter.

53
00:03:02,340 --> 00:03:05,840
So the shop should use a compound bar chart.

54
00:03:05,890 --> 00:03:09,860
This dual bar chart shows rainfall, in millimetres.

55
00:03:09,910 --> 00:03:13,340
Town A had 70 in January and 50 in February.

56
00:03:13,390 --> 00:03:17,360
Town B had 90 in January and 40 in February.

57
00:03:17,410 --> 00:03:20,660
Which town had more rain in total?

58
00:03:20,710 --> 00:03:23,180
Town A: 70 plus 50 is 120.

59
00:03:23,230 --> 00:03:26,250
Town B: 90 plus 40 is 130.

60
00:03:26,300 --> 00:03:31,240
Town B had more rain in total, even though it had less in February.

61
00:03:31,290 --> 00:03:33,570
A compound bar shows fruit sold.

62
00:03:33,620 --> 00:03:36,630
The lower section, for apples, reaches 24.

63
00:03:36,680 --> 00:03:38,460
The whole bar reaches 45.

64
00:03:38,510 --> 00:03:41,590
How many pears does the upper section show?

65
00:03:41,640 --> 00:03:43,270
Here is Wren's working.

66
00:03:43,320 --> 00:03:45,860
Which line goes wrong first?

67
00:03:45,910 --> 00:03:47,120
Line 2 is wrong.

68
00:03:47,170 --> 00:03:50,720
45 is the total for apples and pears together.

69
00:03:50,770 --> 00:03:54,490
The pears section starts at 24, not at 0.

70
00:03:54,540 --> 00:03:56,500
45 minus 24 is 21.

71
00:03:56,550 --> 00:03:59,180
There are 21 pears.

72
00:03:59,230 --> 00:04:03,360
An Olympic medal table is often drawn as a compound bar chart.

73
00:04:03,410 --> 00:04:07,750
Each country's bar is split into gold, silver and bronze.

74
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:13,410
Weather websites use dual bar charts to compare 2 cities, month by month.

75
00:04:13,460 --> 00:04:16,360
Before you read any chart, look for the key.

76
00:04:16,410 --> 00:04:19,320
It tells you what each colour means.

77
00:04:19,370 --> 00:04:20,510
One last question.

78
00:04:20,560 --> 00:04:25,760
To show totals and parts, do you use a compound bar chart, or a dual bar chart?

79
00:04:25,810 --> 00:04:28,950
Pause the video and answer.

80
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:30,340
A compound bar chart.

81
00:04:30,390 --> 00:04:35,720
The height of the whole bar is the total, and the sections are the parts.

82
00:04:35,770 --> 00:04:39,420
To remember: a dual bar chart has bars side by side.

83
00:04:39,470 --> 00:04:41,460
It compares 2 groups.

84
00:04:41,510 --> 00:04:44,140
A compound bar chart has stacked parts.

85
00:04:44,190 --> 00:04:46,480
It shows totals and parts.

86
00:04:46,530 --> 00:04:49,390
Use a clear scale, labels and a key.

87
00:04:49,440 --> 00:04:53,440
For a stacked section, take the top minus the bottom.

88
00:04:53,490 --> 00:04:58,830
Great work! Now practise lesson 16.2 on Camday.
